   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reduction, avoidance of emissions of POPs to air from point and non-point sources [g-TEQ].</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicators and targets are based on the assumption that the establishment of the centralized treatment facility (CTF) for health care waste treatment using BAT technology, will reduce UPOPs releases.  
The 2005 NIP (base year 2003) indicated that medical waste incineration in Mauritius was responsible for 5.5 g-TEQ/year, representing 20% of UPOPs releases in the country.
Since 2005, no NIP update has taken place. A NIP update is planned for 2020/2021 and UPOPs emissions monitoring is planned as part of the NIP update, after which adjusted UPOPs release data can be used as a baseline.</narrative>
    </description>
